Subject: [PATCH v1 0/2] media: i2c: add Sony IMX616 sensor driver
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Sony IMX616 is a 32MP Quad Bayer CMOS image sensor connected over a
4-lane MIPI CSI-2 D-PHY bus. It is the front camera of the Samsung Galaxy
A52 4G (a52q, SM7125).

This series adds a device tree binding and a V4L2 sub-device driver for
it, built on the v4l2-cci register accessors. The register tables were
decoded from the vendor CamX sensor module. Two binned output modes are
supported (3264x2448 at 30 fps and 1632x1224 up to 120 fps).

Tested on the Galaxy A52 with libcamera (simple pipeline, camss) on a
downstream 6.14 kernel; the register tables are unchanged since.

